# Configure and secure

**Prerequisites:** a standalone app directory or `rocci.toml` next to the entry.
**You will do:** validate configuration and change only the fields you understand.
**Verify:** `cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- validate` exits 0.
**Next:** [Package and deploy](/docs/how-to/package-and-deploy/) or
[Configuration](/docs/reference/configuration/).

Unknown fields are errors. The complete-shape example on the reference page is
illustrative; the field tables are canonical.

## Validate

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- validate
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- validate path/to/rocci.toml
```

`ROCCI_CONFIG` overrides the path.

## Local HTTP boundary

`[http].host` is `127.0.0.1` or `localhost` only. `0.0.0.0` is a validation
error. Container bind address is `ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_HOST`, not this field.
`port = 0` means ephemeral. Trailing-slash policy is
`redirect_trailing_slash` (308 when true; 404 with a hint when false).

## Origins and CSP

`[security].allowed_origins` is an explicit `http(s)` list. Default CSP includes
`'unsafe-eval'` because Datastar uses `Function`. Override CSP only when you
can name every source.

## Pin Datastar

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- datastar pin 1.0.2 --app examples/rocci/standalone/counter
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- datastar update --app examples/rocci/standalone/counter
```

`run` does not auto-upgrade. `[assets].datastar = true` is invalid; use a
version string or `false`.

**Related:** [Security model](/docs/concepts/security-model/).
